], "best_idea":"One roll per use against a chance band chosen by how far the skill sits below the thing used, with a hard cap of 5 x level on every skill, is a small data-driven progression rule a fast MMO can run per action.", "decision":"adapt", "decision_why":"Keep the band-and-cap shape and the one-roll-per-use rule for skill rows; change the roll to the engine's seeded stream so the server and replays agree; express chances as plain percent rows. The gain rule stays in the engine, not in rows, and the many-on-one roll rate needs a per-fight cap.", "decision_status":"proposed", "acceptance":"Server test: at level 10 with skill 50 (cap 50) a use gives no gain; a gather node at required level 100 with skill 160 uses the green band (25 percent) from its row; at 130 it uses yellow (75 percent); the same seed over 1000 uses gives identical skill values on two runs."}
